# Fork-local merge policy.
#
# README.md is intentionally rewritten in this fork to describe the fork
# itself and point at upstream for the full documentation. It will therefore
# never agree with upstream's README, and every `git merge upstream/main`
# that touches it would stop on a conflict whose resolution is always
# "keep ours".
#
# The `ours` merge driver makes that automatic. It is NOT built in — each
# clone must enable it once:
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# Without that config git falls back to a normal conflict, so forgetting it
# is safe, just noisier.
#
# Note this file is committed only on this fork's main. Topic branches that
# get proposed upstream branch from the pre-fork history and never carry it,
# so upstream PRs stay free of fork-local policy.
README.md merge=ours
